.TH JUMBLE2 6.SH NAMEjumble2 \- unscramble words against the clock.SH SYNOPSIS\fBjumble2\fR[\-s].SH DESCRIPTIONIt offers directions, then asks the level --\fBE\fRxpert,\fR\fBH\fRard,\fR\fBM\fRoderate\fRor\fBS\fRimple,\fRthen RETURN -- and how many words.  Each word arrives scrambled with thetime you have for it; type it unscrambled and RETURN.  While a word isup,\fB?\fRshows it again with the time left,\fBp\fRpasses and\fBq\fRforfeits.  At least four words are needed to reach the top ten, and eachword after the fourth earns extra time.  After a round RETURN playsagain and\fBc\fRchanges the level.  By Dan Heller, 1988..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-s\fRshow the top ten and leave..SH FILES.TP 12\fB/dd/GAMES/JUMBLE2/scores\fRthe top ten..SH SEE ALSOjumble, anagram